    "caveats": [
      "Confirm the lymphatic shear target (0.01–0.1 Pa) against primary LEC literature — the registry defaults to the HUVEC blood-microvascular range (0.1–1.0 Pa), which is ~10× higher than true lymphatic shear.",
      "Use primary lymphatic endothelial cells (LECs) rather than HUVEC if the goal is lymphatic-specific biology; HUVEC is a blood-endothelial surrogate.",
      "Lymphatic flow is intermittent/oscillatory in vivo; a steady 2 µL/min approximates the time-averaged shear but does not capture pulsatility — consider a rocking or pulsatile protocol if oscillatory shear index matters.",
      "Verify the channel culture area (0.08 cm² assumes a 400 µm × 20 mm footprint) matches the actual device before seeding.",
      "Check medium viscosity; serum-containing medium can be 0.9–1.1e-3 Pa·s, shifting shear by ~±10%."
    ]
